# --- s037 Book I d.8 q.5 = Ord. I d.8 p.2 q.un.
n("n619","s037-01","Quinta questio octaue distinctionis","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 2 q. un., *utrum solus Deus sit immutabilis*. Scotus's long treatment there of the philosophers' necessitarian emanation and of divine contingent causation is what Gorris summarises below (§§s037-04–07).","certain")
n("n620","s037-01","tactus dolore cordis intrinsecus","la","source","Gen. 6:6 (Vulg.): *et tactus dolore cordis intrinsecus*.","certain")
n("n621","s037-01","ego deus et non mutor","la","source","Mal. 3:6 (Vulg.): *ego enim Dominus et non mutor*. Gorris (or his source) has *deus* for *Dominus*.","certain")
n("n622","s037-02","ponitur opinio Henrici quodlibeto. 8. q. 9.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* VIII q. 9 (on whether a creature could be from eternity): the ten modes of having being. Gorris's list is to be checked against Henry's text. As printed, the sixth mode (*ex se possibile… et non est ab alio tamen necesse esse*) looks self-contradictory and may be corrupt.","to-verify")
n("n623","s037-02","Decem modos ponit Henricus","la","textual","This sentence repeats the preceding one almost word for word; *Decē* is underlined in A by a later hand. It may be a printed doublet of a marginal heading.","to-verify")
n("n624","s037-03","⟨quodlibetus⟩","la","textual","A prints *quodlibet⁹ ei⁹. 6⁹.*, with the *-us* sign on all three words. The grammar of *eiusdem quodlibetus eius* is defective; the sense is plainly ‘Henry's *Quodl.* VI, last question’. Reading kept as printed and flagged.","uncertain")
n("n625","s037-03","quodlibetum sextum. q. vlt.","la","source","Henry, *Quodl.* VI (the last question, on the modes in which the heavens might be from the First). Gorris's remark that ‘in our Doctor’ the list sometimes has ten and sometimes four modes is notable. It points to variant textual states of Scotus's d. 8 p. 2 (*Ordinatio* vs *Reportatio*/*Lectura*?), which Gorris explains by Henry's two quodlibets.","to-verify")
n("n626","s037-04","in summa articulo. 54. q. 3.","la","source","Henry, *Summa* a. 54 q. 3 (?). To be checked.","to-verify")
n("n627","s037-04","⟨doctoris⟩","la","textual","A has *doctous* with a superscript, probably *doctoris*. The syntax of the sentence (*est doctoris contra Henricum quasi sibi contradiceret*) is loose.","uncertain")
n("n628","s037-05","ex distinctione secunda. q. 1.","la","source","Cross-reference to *Ord.* I d. 2 p. 1 qq. 1–2 (infinity of God proved from the intellect's knowing infinitely many things distinctly: the *via eminentiae/intellectus*). Cf. §§ on d. 2 above.","certain")
n("n629","s037-06","Nam sequerentur multa inconuenientia.","la","source","Cf. *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 2 q. un. nn. 275–299 (against necessary emanation). Gorris's list of six absurdities is his own ordering of Scotus's arguments, and the order is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n630","s037-07","in secundo dis. 7. et in. 4°.","la","source","*Ord.* II d. 7 q. un. (whether the bad angel necessarily wills ill), and *Ord.* IV d. 49 (beatitude: the impeccability of the blessed).","to-verify")
n("n631","s037-07","indisciplinati est querere omnium causas. 4°. metha.","la","source","Aristotle, *Metaph.* IV 4, 1006a6–8: it is *apaideusia* (*indisciplinatio*) to seek a demonstration of everything. Scotus uses it in *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 2 n. 300 (*quare voluntas voluit hoc, nulla est causa nisi quia voluntas est voluntas*). A later hand repeats the phrase in A's margin.","to-verify")
n("n632","s037-07","7. ethicorum in fine.","la","source","Aristotle, *EN* VII 14, 1154b24–28: God always enjoys a single and simple pleasure (*Deus semper unam et simplicem gaudet delectationem*), because our nature is not simple.","certain")
n("n633","s037-06","non agit de necessario","la","historical","A later hand in A's margin summarises: *deus non agit de necessario…*, with references (partly illegible).")
n("n634","s037-05","turning","en","translation","*versio*: change as a ‘turning’ (cf. Jas. 1:17, *transmutatio… vicissitudinis obumbratio*). The sense of *immutatio que est versio* is somewhat obscure.","uncertain")
n("n635","s037-07","ancient will","en","translation","*voluntate antiqua*: Augustine's phrase (*Conf.* XII 15.18; *De civ. Dei* XII 17), a new effect from an eternal will.")

# --- B collation (full): B52L–B53R
upd("n623", append=" B has the same doublet (*Decem modos ponit Hen. existendi res in qli. viij. q. ix.*), so it was in the common source.")
upd("n624", append=" B reads *quolibet⁹ eiusdē. lxix. q. vl.* (B checked): it has the same *-us* form, and its numeral is corrupt. This confirms that the form goes back to the common source.")
n("n966","s037-03","vbi contentus est","la","textual","B: *vbi causatus est*. A's *contentus* (‘is content with’) gives good sense, and the translation follows A.","certain")
n("n967","s037-03","quodlibetum octauum. q. 9.","la","textual","B: *qlibetum viij. q. iij.* (B checked), against A's *q. 9* here and both texts' *q. ix* in §s037-02.","certain")
upd("n627", append=" B reads *est doctoris* in full, which confirms the reading.", status="verified")
n("n968","s037-06","mouerent in non tempore","la","textual","B: *ponerentur in non tempore*.","certain")
upd("n631", append=" B omits the reference *4°. metha.* and the following *vel* (*querere omnes causas. quia velle dei…*).")
n("n969","s037-07","licet essentia sit prior in essendo","la","textual","B: *licet essentialiter sit prior in essentia*.","certain")
n("n970","s037-07","gaudet voluptate","la","textual","B: *gaudet voluntate*, a slip (Aristotle's *delectatio*).","certain")
